"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_repo_brand=self.webpackChunk_repo_brand||[]).push([[748],{"./stories/guide/07-qirtas.mdx"(__unused_webpack_module,__webpack_exports__,__webpack_require__){__webpack_require__.r(__webpack_exports__),__webpack_require__.d(__webpack_exports__,{default:()=>MDXContent});__webpack_require__("../../node_modules/next/dist/compiled/react/index.js");var jsx_runtime=__webpack_require__("../../node_modules/next/dist/compiled/react/jsx-runtime.js"),lib=__webpack_require__("../../node_modules/@mdx-js/react/lib/index.js"),blocks=__webpack_require__("../../node_modules/@storybook/addon-docs/dist/blocks.js");function _createMdxContent(props){return(0,jsx_runtime.jsxs)(jsx_runtime.Fragment,{children:[(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(blocks.W8,{title:"Guide/Qirtas"}),"\n",(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(blocks.oz,{children:"# Qirtas\n\nThe Society's paper. Its name, «قرطاس», is the paper of our motto: AUIB's paper of news, letters and art, online all year and printed each Edition.\n\nThe front page: the masthead, the dateline between ink rules, the six sections, a lead story and a column of headlines. No empty image boxes: a story without a picture gets a typographic layout.\n\n## The masthead\n\n- \"Qirtas\" in Ubuntu Medium (500), set tight, never Light, never in crimson. On Arabic pages, «قرطاس» in Ubuntu Arabic Bold.\n- Under it, the dateline between two ink rules: the date, the line \"AUIB's paper of news, letters and art\" and the Edition.\n- Then the six sections as a row of text links, always in this order. No logo inside the masthead: the site header already carries it.\n- Qirtas pages sit on paper (`surface-reading`), the one place the page is not white.\n\n## The six sections\n\n| Section | What it carries |\n| --- | --- |\n| News | Reports, features, interviews, profiles, event coverage and explainers. |\n| Voices | Reviews of books, films, plays and exhibitions; columns, opinion essays, letters to the editor, debates and recommendations. |\n| Letters | Poetry, fiction, creative nonfiction, drama, translation and Six Words. |\n| Gallery | Art, photography, illustration, comics, calligraphy and photo essays. |\n| Video | Next Stop, Qirtas's video show, filmed on the AUIB bus; reels, short films, video reports, recorded performances and animation. |\n| Games | Crosswords, quizzes, word ladders, riddles, anagrams and Name the book. |\n\nAlso from Qirtas: **the Edition**, one a semester, curated from Letters and Gallery and printed; **the Sunday Paper**, the members' newsletter, monthly, on the first Sunday.\n\n## Reading Qirtas\n\nHeadlines in Ubuntu, reading in Literata. Every article page is built the same way, so the words do the work.\n\n| Part | Set in |\n| --- | --- |\n| Headline | Ubuntu Light, display, in ink |\n| Dek | Literata 22 / 1.5 (`read-dek`) |\n| Byline | The section in accent, then the author and date: \"Letters · By … · Tuesday, November 17\". Never above the headline. |\n| Body | Literata 17.5 / 1.68 (`read-body`), 60–70 characters a line |\n| Drop cap | Literata Medium in accent, first paragraph only |\n| Pull quote | Ubuntu Light 34 px, one italic accent word |\n| Six Words | Ubuntu Mono, between hairlines |\n\n## Editions\n\n- One curated Edition a semester, from Letters and Gallery, printed and online, on paper with the masthead on the cover; the lockup small at the foot.\n- **Launch Night:** each Edition opens in a room, with readings; its posts use the crimson ground.\n- The call for an Edition is a post; how to submit is a carousel.\n- **Read blind:** every piece is read without its author's name. Arabic and English pieces run in their own editions of the page.\n"})]})}function MDXContent(props={}){const{wrapper:MDXLayout}={...(0,lib.R)(),...props.components};return MDXLayout?(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(MDXLayout,{...props,children:(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_createMdxContent,{...props})}):_createMdxContent()}}}]);
